      "question_id": "math-020",
      "subject": "JEE Mathematics",
      "question_text": "Explain the difference between independent events and mutually exclusive events in probability.",
      "rubric_points": [
        "Independent events: occurrence of one does not affect the probability of the other, P(A\u2229B)=P(A)P(B)",
        "Mutually exclusive events: cannot occur at the same time, P(A\u2229B)=0",
        "Notes that two events with nonzero probability can't be both independent and mutually exclusive"
